Description: caching news server for USENET news (NNTP)
 NewsCache acts like a news server towards news reading clients, but it
 stores only the articles that at least one client has asked for. It gets
 group lists and articles from one or more upstream news servers, optionally
 over TLS, and so saves network bandwidth and load on those servers. Each
 upstream server can be used cached, not cached or offline.
 .
 The shipped /etc/newscache.conf reads from news.blueworldhosting.com and
 lets no client in until a Client entry or a login is added.
